{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"healthful-childlike-aruanas","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nThis is deliverable 2 + the sunset half of deliverable 3 (its red proof).\n\n## Depends on `fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7`\n\nThat story establishes how a new blocking criterion is authored and registered. This one\nreuses that pattern and edits the same routing file, so running them in parallel would\nconflict textually and would also duplicate the grounding work.\n\n## The gap\n\nThe mechanism ratchet is asymmetric. It blocks ADDING a mechanism and never verifies that\na mechanism intended to be temporary was actually REMOVED. Removal always passes, because\na removed mechanism buckets as `stale`. That asymmetry is deliberate — it is what makes\nthe ratchet a ratchet rather than a freeze — but it leaves cutover residue unpoliced.\n\nThe residue is not hypothetical. The complexity-reduction program deleted, among others:\nthe reconciler rollback toggle `REBAR_RECONCILER_WRITE_FACADE`, HMAC left behind after the\nop-cert cutover, the single-pass review demo, alias tombstones, the\n`_engine_support/resolver` shim, and `_call_with_retry`. In each case no acceptance\ncriterion ever said \"old path deleted\", so each one passed its own completion gate with\nthe old path still in place.\n\n## The change\n\nTwo parts, and the second is what gives the first teeth.\n\n1. **The `# mechanism-ok:` marker gains a sunset ticket.** A marker admitting a mechanism\n   that is temporary names the ticket that will remove it. The existing marker form\n   (`<kind> <name> — <reason or ticket id>`) stays valid for a mechanism that is\n   permanent, so this is additive, not a breaking change to every existing marker.\n\n2. **Completion verification of a named sunset ticket fails while its marker still\n   exists.** Closing the ticket that promised to remove the mechanism is refused\n   deterministically — no LLM call — while the marker is still in the tree. This is what\n   converts a promise into an enforced obligation.\n\nPart 2 is deliberately deterministic rather than a rubric judgement: it is a textual\npresence check with an exact answer, and a deterministic check cannot be talked out of a\nverdict.\n\n## Portability\n\nPer `project.portability`, a check whose only trigger is a specific CI system is not\nportable. The sunset check runs inside completion verification, which is an\noperation-linked in-process path reachable with no CI provider at all. The plan must state\nthat explicitly.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nThe deterministic half involves no model. Any rubric half must not assume a single\nvendor's model or tool-calling syntax.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A `# mechanism-ok:` marker may name a sunset ticket id, and the parser records it.\n      Verified by a test reading the parsed marker back.\n- [ ] A marker WITHOUT a sunset ticket id is still accepted. Verified by a test, so the\n      change is proven additive rather than breaking existing markers.\n- [ ] A marker with a blank reason remains an error. Verified by a test, so the existing\n      invariant is proven preserved.\n- [ ] Closing a ticket named as a sunset ticket is REFUSED while its marker is still\n      present in the tree, and the refusal happens with no LLM call. Verified by a test\n      asserting both the refusal and the absence of a model call.\n- [ ] Closing that ticket SUCCEEDS once the marker is gone. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] RED PROOF: reconstructing the `REBAR_RECONCILER_WRITE_FACADE` toggle's marker and\n      its owning ticket reproduces the refusal, demonstrating the residue would have been\n      caught. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] The check runs with no CI provider present. Verified by a test that exercises it\n      with no CI environment configured.\n- [ ] Existing markers in the tree continue to pass the ratchet unchanged. Verified by\n      `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exiting 0.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Plan grounding\n\nExact file:line citations for the marker parser, the `new`/`increased`/`stale` bucketing,\nthe exit-code decision, and the completion-verification refusal path are being measured\nagainst `origin/main` and will be written into this description before plan review is\nrequested. This ticket is NOT ready for review until that is done.","id":"d68f-4771-ebc1-4ee4","parent_id":"77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Enforce mechanism sunset: markers name a sunset ticket, and that ticket cannot close while the marker remains"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793647951591128729,"uuid":"0777e45a-a87b-4503-bcc7-88e5f91e6457"}